# Picking things in a card's list like files in Explorer (decision 064).

scenario: a click picks one; another click picks another instead
panel shelf files 5
tile shelf                          -> Expanded chosen=none
choose shelf b                      -> chosen=b
choose shelf d                      -> chosen=d

scenario: Ctrl adds and takes away; Shift picks a range from the anchor
panel shelf files 5
tile shelf
choose shelf b                      -> chosen=b
choose shelf d ctrl                 -> chosen=b,d
choose shelf b ctrl                 -> chosen=d
choose shelf a                      -> chosen=a
choose shelf c shift                -> chosen=a,b,c
choose shelf e shift                -> chosen=a,b,c,d,e   # the anchor stays where it was
choose shelf b shift                -> chosen=a,b

scenario: Ctrl+Shift adds a range to what's there
panel shelf files 6
tile shelf
choose shelf a
choose shelf c ctrl                 -> chosen=a,c
choose shelf e shift ctrl           -> chosen=a,c,d,e

scenario: a box, or Ctrl+A, picks a set; only things in the list
panel shelf grid 4
tile shelf
choose-set shelf d b x              -> chosen=b,d   # in the list's order
choose-none                         -> chosen=none

scenario: Esc lets go of the selection first, then closes
panel shelf files 3
tile shelf
choose shelf a
esc                                 -> Expanded chosen=none
esc                                 -> Idle

scenario: the selection goes with its card
panel shelf files 3
panel other
tile shelf
choose shelf a                      -> chosen=a
home                                -> chosen=none
choose shelf a                      -> chosen=none  # not on the shown card: nothing

scenario: a thing that goes is no longer picked
panel shelf files 3
tile shelf
choose shelf a
choose shelf c ctrl                 -> chosen=a,c
panel shelf files 2                 -> chosen=a
